  "limits": [
    "Only the fixed PHP 8.5.12 profile is implemented. Other public PHP versions remain work-package obligations.",
    "The 12 exact built-in and extension declaration gaps require W-29 metadata and remain visible.",
    "i386 pow matches executed oracle cases, not a proof for every x87 CPU or every input. 46 of 200000 instruction-level F2XM1 probes differed from correctly rounded RN64 exp2m1; these differences disappeared after the final RN53 step in tested pow controls.",
    "The i386 fractional path costs about 48 microseconds and 71 KiB per call on this Apple M3 microbenchmark. The existing 64-bit path costs about 6.4 nanoseconds with no allocations. No whole-program performance claim is made.",
    "Existing unsafe reference cases remain blocked in W-13 evidence. No crash, timeout or unexecuted scenario was counted as matching PHP.",
    "Host compile/replay resource errors remain distinct from PHP diagnostics and never become successful parses or unknown constants.",
    "W-17 must integrate these compiler/runtime components before end-to-end PHP and application acceptance."
  ],
  "reproduction": {
    "compile_fixtures": "python3 tools/verify_compile_fixtures.py; fixed images, no network, read-only root, bounded memory/PIDs, exact diagnostics and order",
    "frontend": "tools/frontend_corpus.py extracts the corpus outside the repository; tests/frontend/parse_dump.php produces paired call/source locations. Exact replay environments and local paths are recorded per command.",
    "pow_extra": "Decompress the newpairs.txt.gz, newpow32.txt.gz, intpairs.txt.gz and intpow32.txt.gz artifacts into /tmp/phego-compat-pow-research and restore go_verify_test.go.txt there as go_verify_test.go. Use a Go overlay mapping an absent internal/phpnum/research_verify_test.go to that file, then go test -overlay <overlay.json> ./internal/phpnum -run TestResearchOracle -v. The saved Python generators reproduce the two input sets at that same sandbox path. intpow.php.txt and tests/semantics/w10-ops/pow.php produce corresponding outputs in the pinned i386 image.",
    "encoding_and_depth": "The compressed case files retain source and expected observations; write each source to a uniquely named external corpus/*.php and run tests/frontend/parse_dump.php in each pinned image. Corresponding Go tests are encoding_test.go, encoding_timing_test.go and nesting_test.go.",
    "instruction_probe": "From the repository root: python3 docs/implementation/evidence/compatibility-php8512-20261104/instruction-reproduce.py.txt --repo . --mpfr /path/to/libmpfr.6.dylib (Linux: path to libmpfr.so.6). Requires the existing Docker CLI, the pinned i386 PHP image and MPFR 4.2.2; these are research dependencies only. The script creates a fresh external sandbox, regenerates all 200000 inputs (seed 876532019, exact SHA256 asserted), compiles the saved C probe inside the restricted container, compares every F2XM1 result with MPFR exp2m1 at 64 bits, checks the final +1/RN53 step, and runs all 46 targeted PHP pow controls. A different CPU or translator may produce a different instruction result; the script rejects a different mismatch set instead of declaring equivalence."
  },
